  "// archetypes": "Correlated tuples from real networks (RFC 0019.13 \u00a712.2). Realism is a joint fact: C=3 is a real convolution beside K=64, a 7x7 filter and a 224x224 image, and meaningless beside K=905. Each archetype fixes one coherent geometry -- filter size, dilation and padding together -- and varies stride inside it, because padding is chosen to suit the filter and dilation while stride is chosen independently of both. Between them these cover stride 1/2/4/16, padding 0 through 5, dilation 1 through 4, and group counts from 1 through depthwise.",
  "// neighbourhood": "How a draw may drift and stay a layer. R, S, stride, padding and dilation are all deliberately absent: they form one coupled geometry, and moving any of them alone breaks the pairing the archetypes exist to record -- a 7x7 that drifts to 3x3 while pad stays 3, or a 16x16 patch projection whose stride falls to 1, is valid and is in no network. Coverage of those axes comes from declaring more geometries, not from perturbing one. W repeats the 1 ratio because most images are square and a uniform draw over {1, 1.33, 2} would say otherwise.",
  "// mixture": "Anchors alone memorise a handful of shapes; the wide net alone put 0.04% of ten thousand draws anywhere near a real layer. The exploration share is \u00a75.4's floor -- an engine still has to answer for problems nobody wrote down.",
  "// flops": "2*N*K*P*Q*(C/groups)*R*S, with P and Q the output extents. ceil_div(x, s) is floor((x-1)/s)+1, so ceil_div(H + 2*pad - dil*(R-1), stride) is the standard floor((H + 2*pad - dil*(R-1) - 1)/stride) + 1 without needing a floor operator. C is divided by groups because each group convolves its own slice.",
  "flops": {
    "*": [
      2,
      "$q.N",
      "$q.K",
      {
        "ceil_div": [
          {
            "-": [
              {
                "+": [
                  "$q.H",
                  {
                    "*": [
                      2,
                      "$q.pad_h"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "*": [
                  "$q.dilation_h",
                  {
                    "-": [
                      "$q.R",
                      1
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "$q.stride_h"
        ]
      },
      {
        "ceil_div": [
          {
            "-": [
              {
                "+": [
                  "$q.W",
                  {
                    "*": [
                      2,
                      "$q.pad_w"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "*": [
                  "$q.dilation_w",
                  {
                    "-": [
                      "$q.S",
                      1
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "$q.stride_w"
        ]
      },
      {
        "/": [
          "$q.C",
          "$q.groups"
        ]
      },
      "$q.R",
      "$q.S"
    ]
  },
  "// elements": "Input (N*C*H*W) + filter (K*(C/groups)*R*S) + output (N*K*P*Q). Element count across every tensor the operation touches, inputs and outputs. Dtype-free on purpose: bytes is elements times the dtype width, and the width table belongs to the tool rather than repeated as a nested dtype lookup in seven declarations. gbs = bytes / measured time, which is the metric that ranks a memory-bound kernel where tflops cannot.",
  "elements": {
    "+": [
      {
        "*": [
          "$q.N",
          "$q.C",
          "$q.H",
          "$q.W"
        ]
      },
      {
        "*": [
          "$q.K",
          {
            "/": [
              "$q.C",
              "$q.groups"
            ]
          },
          "$q.R",
          "$q.S"
        ]
      },
      {
        "*": [
          "$q.N",
          "$q.K",
          {
            "ceil_div": [
              {
                "-": [
                  {
                    "+": [
                      "$q.H",
                      {
                        "*": [
                          2,
                          "$q.pad_h"
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "*": [
                      "$q.dilation_h",
                      {
                        "-": [
                          "$q.R",
                          1
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "$q.stride_h"
            ]
          },
          {
            "ceil_div": [
              {
                "-": [
                  {
                    "+": [
